  "shared_implementation": "The versioned core protocol and shared LanguageService facade use both existing authenticated native adapters. One native host issues and verifies result-bound analysis contexts.",
  "contract": [
    "Intelligence protocol 2 carries optional bounded analysis contexts. Plugin API 9 and syntax protocol 1 remain separate.",
    "Contexts bind the normalized result digest, original service, client/document/language/path/revision/source, observed source generation and overlay epoch. Stateless HMAC proofs expire after 300 seconds and service replacement resets the key.",
    "Validation checks the exact retained original service without an LSP RPC, new overlays or a replacement process. The shared facade rejects changed result data before preparing authority.",
    "Source-generation changes discard mutable opaque handles before resolution. Incomplete observation retains ordinary read-only analysis without a proof; speculation and edit-producing queries reject incomplete coverage.",
    "Live protocol 1 requests reject. Schema 65 fences older readers; archived protocol 1 action reviews remain recoverable without rewriting their input."
  ],
  "coverage": [
    "Full seven-crate native tests and frontend native tests on macOS and Linux.",
    "Strict native all-target Clippy on both hosts, plus WASI backend, all-target WASM frontend and Windows bridge cross-compilation on macOS.",
    "Targeted optimized Chrome language_plugins and local_bridge component suites.",
    "Installed public-package HTTP regressions exercise paired-local and backend-auth routes, result tampering, changed dependencies, successful original-service validation and absence of extra LSP requests or restarts.",
    "Both facade profiles check result binding before authority, and both stored action modes recover real schema-64 protocol-1 records through schema 65."
  ],
